<title>UK: SAFA sets $90 million three-year bond.</title>
<headline>SAFA sets $90 million three-year bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond was announced by joint lead managers IBJ International and New Japan Securities Europe.</p>
<p> BORROWER   SOUTH AUSTRALIA GOVERNMENT FINANCING AUTHORITY</p>
<p>GUARANTOR  TREASURER OF STATE OF AUSTRALIA</p>
<p> AMT    $90 MLN	 COUPON     5.51	MATURITY    18.NOV.99</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  PAR	 REOFFER     =</p>
<p> FULL FEES  1.20	LISTING    UNLISTED  PAY FREQ    SEMI-ANN</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  =	   DENOMS (K) 10	  SALE LIMS US/UK/AU/JP</p>
<p> NEG PLG    NO	  CRS DEFLT  YES	 FORCE MAJ   YES</p>
<p> MGT/UND    0.20	SELL CONC  1.00	PRAECIPUUM  =</p>
<p> NOTES	LAUNCHED OFF SAFA'S DEBT INSTRUMENT PROGRAMME.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
